steps.prompt:
A customer's message and their order:
{{brief}}

Say which it is: WITHDRAWAL (they changed their mind), DEFECT, WRONG ITEM, LATE or OTHER. Then what they are owed under EU consumer rules: a withdrawal within 14 days of delivery gets a refund of the price and the standard delivery cost, within 14 days of the cancellation, once the goods are back; a defect within the 2-year legal guarantee gets a repair or replacement, or a price cut or refund when that is not possible; a wrong item is replaced or refunded at our cost. Count the days from the dates given. Put the word REFUND on its own line when money goes back. Say what is unclear.

The customer wrote:
{{brief}}

What applies: {{step 1}}

Write the reply: say sorry where we are at fault, say exactly what happens next (return address or label as [placeholder], replacement, refund and when), and ask for anything that is missing, like a photo of a defect. Plain and kind, at most 150 words, in the customer's language.
